Barretenberg: v6.0.0, commit 0219f11d8133970df3974fe5ae65e006bf8c193a,
Apache-2.0, Copyright Aztec Labs and contributors.
https://github.com/AztecProtocol/aztec-packages/tree/0219f11d8133970df3974fe5ae65e006bf8c193a/barretenberg
Statically linked with logging disabled by the application environment hooks.
Barretenberg v5.0.0, commit 7aa2bd616d632801fe65d97ee8a4434f26886b40 (same
license), is statically linked into the separate libdiw_bb5 library
(native/zkpassport-bb5), which only verifies zkPassport proofs of circuits
before 0.22.0 and ships as an optional component.
https://github.com/AztecProtocol/aztec-packages/tree/7aa2bd616d632801fe65d97ee8a4434f26886b40/barretenberg
Both builds use the BB_LITE configuration (no LMDB, world state or IPC) and
x86_64 objects target x86-64-v2 instead of upstream's Skylake default. Their
pinned build dependencies include msgpack-c (Boost Software License 1.0),
libdeflate v1.24 (MIT, 96836d7d9d10e3e0d53e6edb54eb908514e336c4) and Tracy
headers (BSD-3-Clause, 5d542dc09f3d9378d005092a4ad446bd405f819a); the
upstream CMake files pin these sources.
The BN254 CRS is the public Aztec Ignition ceremony transcript prefix, not a
secret setup key. Runtime never downloads it; exact hashes are in assets.json.
